<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin">
    <link rel="shortcut icon" href="static/favicon.ico">
    <title>Privacy: Brailled editor</title>
    <style>
      body { margin: 0; background: #fff; color: #0b2545; font: 1.0625rem/1.6 system-ui, sans-serif; }
      main { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 3rem; }
      h1, h2 { line-height: 1.25; }
      h2 { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
      a { color: #0a4a80; font-weight: bold; }
      a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #0a4a80; outline-offset: 2px; }
      li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <p><a href="./">Open the editor</a></p>
      <h1>Privacy in the Brailled editor</h1>
      <p>This page says what the online editor keeps and what it sends to other services.</p>

      <h2>Before you sign up</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>If you are a child, ask a parent or guardian first. Whoever offers the editor to children needs their
          consent.</li>
        <li>Do not say or type your name or other personal details to Mboni, the AI helper.</li>
        <li>You do not need an account to build, run or save projects.</li>
        <li>Everything Mboni does can be left unused: the editor works with the keyboard.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>If you do not sign in</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your project stays in your browser. It is saved only when you save it, to your own device.</li>
        <li>If you use spoken commands, your browser's speech service hears you. In Chrome that is Google.</li>
        <li>Library pictures and sounds are loaded from Scratch's servers. Some extensions, such as Text to Speech
          and Translate, send what a project gives them to online services.</li>
        <li>Nothing is sent to an AI.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What your account keeps</h2>
      <p>Accounts are kept with Supabase, in the European Union (Ireland). Signing in with Google tells Google that
        you signed in.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The name and email address Google gives.</li>
        <li>Your role, any limits on your account, and how much you use each day.</li>
        <li>For each AI request: its time, kind, AI model, whether it worked, and its estimated cost.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Brailled does not keep what you say, type or build, and does not record your voice.</p>

      <h2>What is sent when you use Mboni</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Typed or spoken requests:</strong> your words or a recording of them, the selected sprite's
          program, the names in your project and the recent conversation go through Brailled's server on Supabase to
          OpenRouter and the company that runs the AI model.</li>
        <li><strong>Live voice:</strong> while it is on, your microphone's sound goes straight from your browser to
          OpenAI, with the program, names and recent conversation. A red dot shows that the microphone is open.</li>
        <li><strong>Reading replies aloud:</strong> the words of a reply may be sent to an online voice service
          through OpenRouter.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>OpenRouter is asked to use only providers that do not keep or collect what is sent. That setting does not
        cover live voice, and Brailled cannot check any provider's promises. Their own terms apply.</p>

      <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
      <p>Your sign-in and your voice settings, including a first name if you typed one. On a shared computer, sign
        out when you finish, and use "Reset for new student" in Voice settings.</p>

      <h2>Your information and questions</h2>
      <p>To ask what is kept about you, or to have your account removed, contact Brailled Education through
        <a href="https://brailledu.bunifuyouths.org/">brailledu.bunifuyouths.org</a>.</p>

      <h2>Source code</h2>
      <p>This editor is free software under the GNU Affero General Public License.
        <a href="<%= htmlWebpackPlugin.options.sourceUrl %>">Read the code of this version</a>. It is built from the
        Scratch editor, and is not made or endorsed by the Scratch Foundation.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
